# Theme colors

Set color only with a variable from `src/styles/colors.css`. Do not write a new hex, rgb, hsl, or named color in CSS, inline styles, or canvas fills.

Use the existing `--ft-*` color tokens, including text, surfaces, borders, brand, status, sidebar, and chart colors. Light values live on `:root`. Dark values live on `:root[data-theme="dark"]`.

`transparent`, `currentColor`, and `color-mix()` of an existing token are allowed. A new color belongs in `colors.css`, and only when the user asks for one.

In canvas or other APIs that cannot take a variable string, read the computed token. Do not substitute a hex code.

```css
/* BAD */
color: #217d73;
background: rgb(26, 29, 32);

/* GOOD */
color: var(--ft-primary);
background: var(--ft-surface);
```
